Package: ssh3-go-client
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Conflicts: ssh3-client
Replaces: ssh3-client
Description: SSH3 client - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 The SSH3 client of the nagual2 fork (francoismichel/ssh3 lineage):
 the ssh(1)-canon CLI over one HTTP/3 (QUIC) extended CONNECT per
 target - sessions, the -L/-R/-D forwards (the documented udp://
 extension), -J proxy jumps, the control master (-M/-S/-O), the
 agent forwarding (-A), file transfers (ssh3 -transfer, the scp
 analog) and the -f background form; the fork's own long names stay
 as deprecated aliases.
 .
 The first connection pins the server certificate TOFU-style in
 ~/.ssh3/known_hosts (the same store the C implementation reads).
 See ssh3(1).

Package: ssh3-go-server
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 openssl,
 ssh3-go-client (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: ssh3-server
Replaces: ssh3-server
Description: SSH3 server - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 The SSH3 daemon of the nagual2 fork: the SSH3 protocol carried over
 HTTP/3 (QUIC, RFC 9220 extended CONNECT).  Public keys authenticate
 out of the box (authorized_keys or ~/.ssh3/authorized_identities of
 the target account); on amd64 passwords against the unix accounts
 (the CGO crypt backend, enabled by default, SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_
 LOGIN=0 turns it off and the root account always refuses the
 password step).  Reverse forwards honor the GatewayPorts policy;
 the per-user limits and the brute-force lockout are tunable
 through flags and SSH3_* variables read from /etc/ssh3/
 ssh3-server.env.
 .
 The service runs as root with the per-session identity drop (the
 OpenSSH shape), the Debian unit keeps no sandbox directives on
 purpose; the enable/restart cycle rides dh_installsystemd
 (policy 9.3).
 .
 The server depends on the matching ssh3-go-client (the openssh(8)
 canon: one release wave ships both halves together).

Package: ssh3go
Architecture: all
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ssh3-go-client,
 ssh3-go-server
Description: SSH3 - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 (client and server metapackage)
 The openssh(8) `ssh' metapackage analog of this source package:
 installs the ssh3-go-client and ssh3-go-server packages at matching
 versions, so one install brings up the full SSH3 pair - the client
 CLI and the daemon.
